{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659004057,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da032e590026MgPlwLhwtAH8b","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da0326c400156W5m7qxodnQOZ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b25250717a4c4774","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":750,"limit":500},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 750-1249\n750:           log: \"minIterations missing; using no convergence floor for backward compatibility.\"\n751:         if_min_iterations_clamped:\n752:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"configured\":{min_iterations_raw},\"effective\":{effective_min_iterations},\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"message\":\"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n753:           log: \"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\"\n754:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n755:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n756:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n757: \n758:       step_graph_convergence:\n759:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n760:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n761:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n762:         outputs:\n763:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n764:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n765:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n766:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n767:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n768:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n769:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n770: \n771:       step_check_convergence:\n772:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n773:         algorithm: |\n774:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n775:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n776:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n777:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: steps 4 and 5 are telemetry only and cannot set STOP or BLOCKED. Record weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\" and choose a broader next focus.\n778:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n779:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n780:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n781:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n782:                signals = []\n783:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n784:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n785:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n786:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n787:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n788:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n789:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n790:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n791:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n792:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n793:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n794:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n795:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n796:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n797:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n798:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n799:                  stop_blocked = true\n800:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n801:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n802:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n803:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n804:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n805:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n806:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n807:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n808:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n809:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n810:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n811:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n812:                  stop_blocked = false\n813:           6. else: CONTINUE\n814:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n815:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n816:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n817:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n818:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n819:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n820:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n821:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n822:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n823:                if not guardResult.passed:\n824:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n825:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n826:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n827:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n828:         outputs:\n829:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n830:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n831:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n832:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n833:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n834:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n835:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n836:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n837:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n838:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n839:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n840:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n841:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n842:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n843: \n844:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n845:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n846:         if_pass:\n847:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n848:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n849: \n850:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n851:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n852:         if_blocked:\n853:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n854:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n855:           set:\n856:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n857:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n858:             stop_blocked: false\n859: \n860:       step_handle_convergence:\n861:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n862:         if_stop:\n863:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n864:           if_divergent_eligible:\n865:             eligibility_contract:\n866:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n867:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n868:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n869:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n870:             steps:\n871:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n872:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n873:                 command: |\n874:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n875:                   import {\n876:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n877:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n878:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n879:                   import {\n880:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n881:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n882: \n883:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n884:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n885:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n886:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n887:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n888:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n889:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n890:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n891:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n892:                   });\n893:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n894:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n895:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n896:                         seat.id,\n897:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n898:                       ]))\n899:                     : {};\n900:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n901:                     ...prepared,\n902:                     seatPrompts,\n903:                     boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n904:                   })}\\n`);\n905:                   EOF\n906:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n907:                 outputs:\n908:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n909:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n910:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n911:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n912:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n913:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n914:                   - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n915:                   - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n916:                   - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n917:                   - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"\n918:                   - pivot_seat_002_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-002']\"\n919:                   - pivot_seat_003_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-003']\"\n920:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n921:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n922: \n923:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_001:\n924:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the analytical research direction-selection seat\"\n925:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n926:                 capture_timing: true\n927:                 if_native:\n928:                   dispatch:\n929:                     agent: deep-research\n930:                     model: opus\n931:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_001_prompt\"\n932:                   wait_for_completion: true\n933:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_001.\"\n934:                 outputs:\n935:                   - pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n936:                   - pivot_seat_001_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n937:                   - pivot_seat_001_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n938:                   - pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n939:                   - pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n940:                   - pivot_seat_001_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n941: \n942:               step_record_pivot_seat_001:\n943:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-001 native dispatch outcome\"\n944:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n945:                 command: |\n946:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n947:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n948:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status}';\n949:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n950:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_001_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') }\n951:              