{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659035154,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da03a7d1001oshFjANFh3VCPv","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da039f11001qyE53pmDNDumGX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b921a7eb971df7e1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/spec.md"},"output":"Read file specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/spec.md, lines 1-145\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Feature Specification: Phase 1: deep-research\"\n3: description: \"Nobody has mapped how Mistral Vibe could become a governed runtime mode here, or how much of cli-opencode's extension, hook and plugin surface it could carry. This phase researches both and writes the ranked build phases.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"mistral vibe deep research\"\n6:   - \"phase 1 deep research\"\n7:   - \"vibe opencode feature parity research\"\n8: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n9: contextType: \"research\"\n10: ---\n11: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n12: # Feature Specification: Phase 1: deep-research\n13: \n14: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n15: ---\n16: \n17: <!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n18: ## 1. METADATA\n19: \n20: | Field | Value |\n21: |-------|-------|\n22: | **Level** | 1 |\n23: | **Priority** | P1 |\n24: | **Status** | Draft |\n25: | **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n26: | **Branch** | `main` |\n27: | **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n28: | **Phase** | 1 of 3 |\n29: | **Predecessor** | None |\n30: | **Successor** | 002-mistral-provider-roster |\n31: | **Handoff Criteria** | `research/research.md` and `research/phase-plan.md` exist, and the plan names the build phases that follow phase 003 |\n32: <!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n37: ## Phase Context\n38: \n39: This is **Phase 1** of the Mistral as a provider across the CLI runtimes and Mistral Vibe as a cli-external-orchestration runtime mode specification.\n40: \n41: **Scope Boundary**: Read-only research of the Vibe source, a local Vibe install and this repository's runtime surfaces, written only under `research/`.\n42: \n43: **Dependencies**:\n44: - A local `mistral-vibe` install for read-only commands, which waits on the operator's yes.\n45: - `research-angles.md` as the brief.\n46: \n47: **Deliverables**:\n48: - `research/research.md`, with a parity table against cli-opencode.\n49: - `research/phase-plan.md`, ranking the build phases.\n50: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: <!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n55: ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n56: \n57: ### Problem Statement\n58: Mistral Vibe is Mistral's own coding agent and the client its subscription is built around, but this repository has no mode for it. Its headless contract, configuration, hook system and fit with the deep-loop fan-out are unknown, so no build phase can be scoped without guessing.\n59: \n60: ### Purpose\n61: Decide whether Vibe can be a governed runtime mode, how far it can match cli-opencode's extensions, hooks and plugins, and in which order to build it.\n62: <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n63: \n64: <!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n65: ### Measured Behavior\n66: ```text\n67: $ command -v vibe; ls ~/.vibe\n68: (no output: Vibe is not installed on this machine)\n69: $ rg -n -i 'vibe' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration --glob '*.md'\n70: (no runtime mode or reference names Vibe)\n71: ```\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n77: ## 3. SCOPE\n78: \n79: ### In Scope\n80: - Work the eight angles in `research-angles.md`.\n81: - Compare every cli-opencode extension, hook and plugin surface with Vibe's, and say what porting each takes.\n82: - Write the synthesis and a ranked phase plan.\n83: \n84: ### Out of Scope\n85: - Building any part of the mode - the build phases come from this phase's plan.\n86: - Writing the operator's `~/.vibe/` or any credential - research stays read-only.\n87: \n88: ### Files to Change\n89: \n90: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n91: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n92: | `research/` | Create | Iterations, synthesis and phase plan |\n93: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n98: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n99: \n100: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n101: \n102: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n103: \n104: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n105: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n106: | REQ-001 | Every angle is answered with cited evidence | `research/research.md` has one section per angle, each claim cited or marked UNKNOWN |\n107: | REQ-002 | The parity table covers every cli-opencode surface the repository uses | Each row says equivalent, partial or none, with the porting cost |\n108: \n109: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n110: \n111: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n112: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n113: | REQ-003 | A ranked phase plan exists | `research/phase-plan.md` lists the build phases with a handoff check for each |\n114: <!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n119: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n120: \n121: - **SC-001**: The phase plan can be scaffolded as children 004 onward of this parent without a new research question.\n122: - **SC-002**: The headless dispatch shape is recorded from a live read-only `vibe --help`, not from documentation alone.\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n128: ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n129: \n130: | Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n131: |------|------|--------|------------|\n132: | Dependency | Local Vibe install | High: angles 1, 3 and 6 need live help output | Install only after the operator's yes; until then mark live claims `documented, unconfirmed` |\n133: | Risk | Vibe versions change fast | Med: v2 and v3 sources disagree on the current version | Pin the installed version in every live capture |\n134: <!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n139: ## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n140: \n141: - Is a print mode or ACP the better dispatch surface for the fan-out?\n142: - Does a Vibe turn draw on the same usage counter as an OpenCode turn on the same key?\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n144: \n145: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/spec.md, lines 1-145\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Feature Specification: Phase 1: deep-research\"\n3: description: \"Nobody has mapped how Mistral Vibe could become a governed runtime mode here, or how much of cli-opencode's extension, hook and plugin surface it could carry. This phase researches both and writes the ranked build phases.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"mistral vibe deep research\"\n6:   - \"phase 1 deep research\"\n7:   - \"vibe opencode feature parity research\"\n8: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n9: contextType: \"research\"\n10: ---\n11: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n12: # Feature Specification: Phase 1: deep-research\n13: \n14: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n15: ---\n16: \n17: <!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n18: ## 1. METADATA\n19: \n20: | Field | Value |\n21: |-------|-------|\n22: | **Level** | 1 |\n23: | **Priority** | P1 |\n24: | **Status** | Draft |\n25: | **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n26: | **Branch** | `main` |\n27: | **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n28: | **Phase** | 1 of 3 |\n29: | **Predecessor** | None |\n30: | **Successor** | 002-mistral-provider-roster |\n31: | **Handoff Criteria** | `research/research.md` and `research/phase-plan.md` exist, and the plan names the build phases that follow phase 003 |\n32: <!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n37: ## Phase Context\n38: \n39: This is **Phase 1** of the Mistral as a provider across the CLI runtimes and Mistral Vibe as a cli-external-orchestration runtime mode specification.\n40: \n41: **Scope Boundary**: Read-only research of the Vibe source, a local Vibe install and this repository's runtime surfaces, written only under `research/`.\n42: \n43: **Dependencies**:\n44: - A local `mistral-vibe` install for read-only commands, which waits on the operator's yes.\n45: - `research-angles.md` as the brief.\n46: \n47: **Deliverables**:\n48: - `research/research.md`, with a parity table against cli-opencode.\n49: - `research/phase-plan.md`, ranking the build phases.\n50: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: <!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n55: ## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n56: \n57: ### Problem Statement\n58: Mistral Vibe is Mistral's own coding agent and the client its subscription is built around, but this repository has no mode for it. Its headless contract, configuration, hook system and fit with the deep-loop fan-out are unknown, so no build phase can be scoped without guessing.\n59: \n60: ### Purpose\n61: Decide whether Vibe can be a governed runtime mode, how far it can match cli-opencode's extensions, hooks and plugins, and in which order to build it.\n62: <!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n63: \n64: <!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n65: ### Measured Behavior\n66: ```text\n67: $ command -v vibe; ls ~/.vibe\n68: (no output: Vibe is not installed on this machine)\n69: $ rg -n -i 'vibe' .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration --glob '*.md'\n70: (no runtime mode or reference names Vibe)\n71: ```\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n77: ## 3. SCOPE\n78: \n79: ### In Scope\n80: - Work the eight angles in `research-angles.md`.\n81: - Compare every cli-opencode extension, hook and plugin surface with Vibe's, and say what porting each takes.\n82: - Write the synthesis and a ranked phase plan.\n83: \n84: ### Out of Scope\n85: - Building any part of the mode - the build phases come from this phase's plan.\n86: - Writing the operator's `~/.vibe/` or any credential - research stays read-only.\n87: \n88: ### Files to Change\n89: \n90: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n91: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n92: | `research/` | Create | Iterations, synthesis and phase plan |\n93: <!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: <!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n98: ## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n99: \n100: REQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n101: \n102: ### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n103: \n104: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n105: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n106: | REQ-001 | Every angle is answered with cited evidence | `research/research.md` has one section per angle, each claim cited or marked UNKNOWN |\n107: | REQ-002 | The parity table covers every cli-opencode surface the repository uses | Each row says equivalent, partial or none, with the porting cost |\n108: \n109: ### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n110: \n111: | ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n112: |----|-------------|---------------------|\n113: | REQ-003 | A ranked phase plan exists | `research/phase-plan.md` lists the build phases with a handoff check for each |\n114: <!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n119: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n120: \n121: - **SC-001**: The phase plan can be scaffolded as children 004 onward of this parent without a new research question.\n122: - **SC-002**: The headless dispatch shape is recorded from a live read-only `vibe --help`, not from documentation alone.\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n128: ## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n129: \n130: | Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n131: |------|------|--------|------------|\n132: | Dependency | Local Vibe install | High: angles 1, 3 and 6 need live help output | Install only after the operator's yes; until then mark live claims `documented, unconfirmed` |\n133: | Risk | Vibe versions change fast | Med: v2 and v3 sources disagree on the current version | Pin the installed version in every live capture |\n134: <!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n139: ## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n140: \n141: - Is a print mode or ACP the better dispatch surface for the fan-out?\n142: - Does a Vibe turn draw on the same usage counter as an OpenCode turn on the same key?\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n144: \n145: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659035089,"end":1794659035154}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659035222,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da03a7cf001YgTyt0V21ZGM0Z","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da039f11001qyE53pmDNDumGX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83a47021583bbf84","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/evidence/vibe-help.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/evidence/vibe-help.txt, lines 1-95\n1: $ vibe --version\n2: vibe 3.1.2\n3: \n4: $ vibe --help\n5: Run the Mistral Vibe interactive CLI\n6: \n7: Usage: vibe [OPTIONS] [INITIAL_PROMPT] [COMMAND]\n8: \n9: Commands:\n10:   mcp     Manage MCP server configuration without starting a session\n11:   config  Describe Vibe's configuration without starting a session\n12:   help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n13: \n14: Arguments:\n15:   [INITIAL_PROMPT]  Initial prompt for the interactive session, or the prompt in headless mode\n16: \n17: Options:\n18:   -v, --version\n19:           Show version and exit\n20:       --workdir <CWD>\n21:           Change to this directory before running [env: VIBE_CWD=]\n22:   -c, --continue\n23:           Continue this terminal's last session in this folder, else the folder's most recent\n24:       --resume [<RESUME>]\n25:           Resume a session. Without SESSION_ID, shows an interactive picker\n26:       --setup\n27:           Setup API key and exit\n28:   -p, --prompt [<PROMPT>]\n29:           Run in headless (programmatic) mode: send prompt, output response, exit\n30:       --output <OUTPUT>\n31:           Output format for headless mode [default: text] [possible values: text, json, streaming]\n32:       --max-turns <MAX_TURNS>\n33:           Maximum number of assistant turns (headless mode only)\n34:       --max-price <MAX_PRICE>\n35:           Maximum cumulative cost in dollars of the run's root session and subagents (headless mode only). A model priced at 0 is free; a limit of 0 stops the run before the next call once any call has cost money\n36:       --max-tokens <MAX_TOKENS>\n37:           Maximum cumulative prompt + completion tokens of the run's root session and subagents (headless mode only)\n38:       --time-limit <SECONDS>\n39:           Interrupt the run once SECONDS have passed since start, write the export and exit 3. SIGTERM stops the run the same way\n40:       --prompt-file <PATH>\n41:           Run in programmatic mode with the prompt read from PATH, instead of -p TEXT or stdin\n42:       --system-prompt-file <PATH>\n43:           Replace Vibe's own system prompt instructions with the text in PATH (headless mode only). Project context and AGENTS.md still follow it\n44:       --output-dir <DIR>\n45:           On every exit, write export.json (Vibe version, effective config, token usage, cost, stop reason, outcome) and a copy of the session journal (session/) to DIR\n46:       --agent <NAME>\n47:           Agent to use (builtin: ask, accept-edits, smart-approve, auto-approve, or custom from ~/.vibe/agents/NAME.toml). Defaults to the 'default_agent' config setting\n48:       --model <ALIAS>\n49:           Model alias to use instead of 'active_model' (headless mode only, new sessions). Not saved as the default\n50:       --auto-approve\n51:           Approves all tool calls without prompting: a new session on a built-in mode starts the auto-approve agent instead [alias: --yolo]\n52:       --smart-approve\n53:           Classify each tool call and auto-run the safe ones, prompting only for risky ones\n54:       --enabled-tools <ENABLED_TOOLS>\n55:           Enable specific tools (headless: disables all others). Repeat the flag\n56:       --disabled-tools <DISABLED_TOOLS>\n57:           Disable specific tools after --enabled-tools filtering. Repeat the flag\n58:       --trust\n59:           Trust the working directory for this invocation only\n60:       --worktree [<WORKTREE>]\n61:           Run inside a git worktree under $VIBE_HOME/worktrees. With NAME, create (or reuse) a worktree and branch named NAME. Without NAME, create a new one named after the prompt (or a random slug). Combines with `-c`/`--resume`: the worktree is prepared first and the resume is then scoped to the worktree directory\n62:       --add-dir <ADD_DIR>\n63:           Additional working directory for file access. Repeat the flag\n64:       --check-upgrade\n65:           Check for a Vibe update now, prompt to install it, and exit\n66:   -h, --help\n67:           Print help\n68: \n69: Commands:\n70:   update         Check for a Vibe update now (same as --check-upgrade).\n71: \n72: $ vibe-acp --help\n73: usage: vibe-acp [-h] [-v] [--setup]\n74: \n75: Run Mistral Vibe in ACP mode\n76: \n77: options:\n78:   -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n79:   -v, --version  show program's version number and exit\n80:   --setup        Setup API key and exit\n81: \n82: $ vibe-app-server --help\n83: usage: vibe-app-server [-h] [--multiplex]\n84:                        [--additional-builtin-plugin-root PATH]\n85: \n86: Run the Mistral Vibe app server\n87: \n88: options:\n89:   -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n90:   --multiplex           Serve isolated Unified Harness connections in one\n91:                         stdio process.\n92:   --additional-builtin-plugin-root PATH\n93:                         Directory to discover built-in plugins from, in\n94:                         addition to the ones shipped inside the package. May\n95:                         be given more than once.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/evidence/vibe-help.txt, lines 1-95\n1: $ vibe --version\n2: vibe 3.1.2\n3: \n4: $ vibe --help\n5: Run the Mistral Vibe interactive CLI\n6: \n7: Usage: vibe [OPTIONS] [INITIAL_PROMPT] [COMMAND]\n8: \n9: Commands:\n10:   mcp     Manage MCP server configuration without starting a session\n11:   config  Describe Vibe's configuration without starting a session\n12:   help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n13: \n14: Arguments:\n15:   [INITIAL_PROMPT]  Initial prompt for the interactive session, or the prompt in headless mode\n16: \n17: Options:\n18:   -v, --version\n19:           Show version and exit\n20:       --workdir <CWD>\n21:           Change to this directory before running [env: VIBE_CWD=]\n22:   -c, --continue\n23:           Continue this terminal's last session in this folder, else the folder's most recent\n24:       --resume [<RESUME>]\n25:           Resume a session. Without SESSION_ID, shows an interactive picker\n26:       --setup\n27:           Setup API key and exit\n28:   -p, --prompt [<PROMPT>]\n29:           Run in headless (programmatic) mode: send prompt, output response, exit\n30:       --output <OUTPUT>\n31:           Output format for headless mode [default: text] [possible values: text, json, streaming]\n32:       --max-turns <MAX_TURNS>\n33:           Maximum number of assistant turns (headless mode only)\n34:       --max-price <MAX_PRICE>\n35:           Maximum cumulative cost in dollars of the run's root session and subagents (headless mode only). A model priced at 0 is free; a limit of 0 stops the run before the next call once any call has cost money\n36:       --max-tokens <MAX_TOKENS>\n37:           Maximum cumulative prompt + completion tokens of the run's root session and subagents (headless mode only)\n38:       --time-limit <SECONDS>\n39:           Interrupt the run once SECONDS have passed since start, write the export and exit 3. SIGTERM stops the run the same way\n40:       --prompt-file <PATH>\n41:           Run in programmatic mode with the prompt read from PATH, instead of -p TEXT or stdin\n42:       --system-prompt-file <PATH>\n43:           Replace Vibe's own system prompt instructions with the text in PATH (headless mode only). Project context and AGENTS.md still follow it\n44:       --output-dir <DIR>\n45:           On every exit, write export.json (Vibe version, effective config, token usage, cost, stop reason, outcome) and a copy of the session journal (session/) to DIR\n46:       --agent <NAME>\n47:           Agent to use (builtin: ask, accept-edits, smart-approve, auto-approve, or custom from ~/.vibe/agents/NAME.toml). Defaults to the 'default_agent' config setting\n48:       --model <ALIAS>\n49:           Model alias to use instead of 'active_model' (headless mode only, new sessions). Not saved as the default\n50:       --auto-approve\n51:           Approves all tool calls without prompting: a new session on a built-in mode starts the auto-approve agent instead [alias: --yolo]\n52:       --smart-approve\n53:           Classify each tool call and auto-run the safe ones, prompting only for risky ones\n54:       --enabled-tools <ENABLED_TOOLS>\n55:           Enable specific tools (headless: disables all others). Repeat the flag\n56:       --disabled-tools <DISABLED_TOOLS>\n57:           Disable specific tools after --enabled-tools filtering. Repeat the flag\n58:       --trust\n59:           Trust the working directory for this invocation only\n60:       --worktree [<WORKTREE>]\n61:           Run inside a git worktree under $VIBE_HOME/worktrees. With NAME, create (or reuse) a worktree and branch named NAME. Without NAME, create a new one named after the prompt (or a random slug). Combines with `-c`/`--resume`: the worktree is prepared first and the resume is then scoped to the worktree directory\n62:       --add-dir <ADD_DIR>\n63:           Additional working directory for file access. Repeat the flag\n64:       --check-upgrade\n65:           Check for a Vibe update now, prompt to install it, and exit\n66:   -h, --help\n67:           Print help\n68: \n69: Commands:\n70:   update         Check for a Vibe update now (same as --check-upgrade).\n71: \n72: $ vibe-acp --help\n73: usage: vibe-acp [-h] [-v] [--setup]\n74: \n75: Run Mistral Vibe in ACP mode\n76: \n77: options:\n78:   -h, --help     show this help message and exit\n79:   -v, --version  show program's version number and exit\n80:   --setup        Setup API key and exit\n81: \n82: $ vibe-app-server --help\n83: usage: vibe-app-server [-h] [--multiplex]\n84:                        [--additional-builtin-plugin-root PATH]\n85: \n86: Run the Mistral Vibe app server\n87: \n88: options:\n89:   -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n90:   --multiplex           Serve isolated Unified Harness connections in one\n91:                         stdio process.\n92:   --additional-builtin-plugin-root PATH\n93:                         Directory to discover built-in plugins from, in\n94:                         addition to the ones shipped inside the package. May\n95:                         be given more than once."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/evidence/vibe-help.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659035087,"end":1794659035222}}}}
