{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659318403,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da07fa050020CxKxRlmJUelty","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da07ddb3001nPOZ1liJDQ2MT5","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba34e582cc71818d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"},"output":"2026-11-14T12:28:38Z\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2026-11-14T12:28:38Z\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659318277,"end":1794659318403}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794659320187,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"id":"prt_1da08017b001bwsr0pWFOeGnke","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da07ddb3001nPOZ1liJDQ2MT5","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"3e6a187e02bae2a73366ab9be7f479ec3b460f21","cost":0.00132291,"tokens":{"input":1641,"output":54,"reasoning":963,"cache":{"read":155520,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794659323457,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"id":"prt_1da080e41001yvHOX8kTqQjrCI","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da080182001X3uBfPfUCC9aOj","type":"step-start","snapshot":"3e6a187e02bae2a73366ab9be7f479ec3b460f21"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659329517,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da080e43001zEIBeKGUr2ek5z","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da080182001X3uBfPfUCC9aOj","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eeed9fcc0db7c9e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: providers, models and the subscription\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 2: how Vibe authenticates, which providers and models a dispatch can pin, how reasoning effort is set, and which usage counter a turn draws on compared with the same model through OpenCode. Scope was kept to source evidence; no key was read and no value was printed.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. A Vibe dispatch has two credential families. The first-party `mistral` provider resolves a browser sign-in (OIDC against `https://console.mistral.ai`) or an API key from `MISTRAL_API_KEY`; any additional `[[providers]]` row is BYOK with its own `api_base` and `api_key_env_var`. First-party code prefers the active provider only when it is a Mistral provider, so a third-party credential never reaches a first-party endpoint. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:137-196] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/_defaults.py:9-19] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/platform_auth/_mistral.py:55-75]\n\n2. Providers are declarative, not a closed list: `ProviderConfig` carries `name`, `api_base`, `api_key_env_var`, browser-auth base URLs, `api_style` (default `openai`), `backend` (`mistral` or `generic`), `project_id`/`region` for Google Vertex ADC, `reasoning_field_name`, `emits_finish_reason` and `extra_headers`. The shipped defaults are only `mistral` and a local `llamacpp` endpoint, so any OpenAI-compatible gateway is a config row. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:137-204] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py:200-214]\n\n3. Models are declarative rows too: `name`, `provider`, `alias`, `temperature` (default 0.2), `thinking`, `thinking_levels`, `input_price`/`output_price`/`cached_input_price` per million tokens, `max_context_length`, `auto_compact_threshold`, `supports_images`. Pinning `deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017` and `zai-glm-5-3-flash` is therefore a provider row plus a model row each, selected by `--model <alias>`; Vibe compiles in no roster beyond the single default `mistral-medium-3.5` row. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:522-616] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py:216-231]\n\n4. The Mistral-side catalogue is fetched, not shipped: `MODEL_CATALOG_PATH = \"/model-catalog\"` with surface `vibe-code`, a 5s bounded fetch and a 30-day cache TTL, built from the provider's `api_base`. A dispatch therefore sees whatever the configured Mistral API base advertises, while BYOK providers rely entirely on declared rows. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/model_catalog/_constants.py:1-27]\n\n5. Reasoning effort has no dispatch flag. It is a per-model config field: `thinking` (a `ThinkingLevel`, default `off`) plus the offered `thinking_levels` list, with `thinking_is_set` distinguishing \"unset\" from \"off\" and the Mistral backend mapping curated level sets to its own reasoning-effort parameter. A governed executor must therefore pin reasoning through the model row or agent profile, not through the command line. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:551-616] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/llm/reasoning.py:17-62]\n\n6. The usage counter is the org's monthly Vibe Code allowance. `GET /v1/billing/subscription` names the plan and whether pay-as-you-go covers the run past its allowance; `GET /v1/billing/budget` reports `usage_percentage`, `initial_budget`, `reset_at` and `payg_enabled` for the Vibe Code budget. Both are optional and read as `None` on a self-hosted platform or missing permission. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_billing.py:1-46]\n\n7. Plan labels are derived from `/whoami`: chat plans map Free/Pro/Student/Team, Mistral Code maps \"Free Codestral\"/\"Code Enterprise\", and API plans map \"Free API\"/\"PAYG API\". The label is display data; the budget read above is the counter a dispatch actually draws on. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/setup/auth/whoami.py:346-390]\n\n8. Per-dispatch cost is locally computable even without the billing API: `export.json` carries `usage`, `cost_usd`, `steps` and `subagents[].cost_usd`, priced from the model row's per-million rates with cached input billed at `cached_input_price` when set. That gives a governed executor a cost signal per run, independent of the org budget endpoint. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/run_export.py:117-160,183-190] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:537-550]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reading `~/.vibe/config.toml` or any key to confirm the live provider: the directory holds only `trusted_folders.toml`, so there is no local provider state to observe, and reading a key value is out of scope by the angle's own rule.\n- Treating the model catalogue as a shipped roster: it is fetched from `/model-catalog` at runtime with a 5s cap and 30-day cache, so an offline install has only declared rows.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Answering the OpenCode-versus-Vibe counter comparison from client code. Both clients send a key to a provider; which internal counter the platform debits is server-side and unobservable locally. Recorded as UNKNOWN with the exact measurement that would settle it.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"subscription\" could mean the chat plan or the Vibe Code budget. Selected the narrow reading: the budget endpoint that the client reads for Vibe Code usage, with plan labels as display only.\n- Contradictory evidence: `--setup` is described as \"Setup API key and exit\", while the provider defaults also offer browser sign-in. Both are real paths; the install has neither configured, so no live discrimination was possible.\n- Missing dependencies: no credential, so the billing read, `/whoami` label and a live model pin could not be observed. Source evidence carried the findings; every live claim is marked unconfirmed.\n- Partial success: the provider/model/auth contract is fully answered; the cross-runtime usage-counter comparison is UNKNOWN.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/_defaults.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/platform_auth/_mistral.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/model_catalog/_constants.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/llm/reasoning.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_billing.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/setup/auth/whoami.py\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/run_export.py\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: Which providers, models and authentication paths can a Vibe dispatch use, and which usage counter does a turn draw on?\n- Questions answered: Which providers, models and authentication paths can a Vibe dispatch use, and which usage counter does a turn draw on? (Vibe side answered; the OpenCode-counter comparison is UNKNOWN, with the measurement that would settle it recorded below.)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: starting from the config schema and `ProviderConfig`/`ModelConfig` gave the whole model surface in two files, and `_billing.py` answered the counter question directly instead of by inference from marketing copy.\n- What did not work and why: looking for a \"subscription\" flag in the CLI. There is none: the plan is read from the platform, not configured locally.\n- What I would do differently: capture `vibe config schema` earlier and query it by definition name; it is the cheapest index to every config field, and it was already on disk from iteration 1's capture.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 3: configuration and the repo-local runtime folder. Read the config layer order (`core/config/layers/`), `AGENTS.md`/project-context handling, agent TOML discovery under `~/.vibe/agents/`, and the path resolution module, then state exactly what a repo-root `.vibe/` mirror would contain.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 2: providers, models and the subscription\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 2: how Vibe authenticates, which providers and models a dispatch can pin, how reasoning effort is set, and which usage counter a turn draws on compared with the same model through OpenCode. Scope was kept to source evidence; no key was read and no value was printed.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. A Vibe dispatch has two credential families. The first-party `mistral` provider resolves a browser sign-in (OIDC against `https://console.mistral.ai`) or an API key from `MISTRAL_API_KEY`; any additional `[[providers]]` row is BYOK with its own `api_base` and `api_key_env_var`. First-party code prefers the active provider only when it is a Mistral provider, so a third-party credential never reaches a first-party endpoint. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:137-196] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/_defaults.py:9-19] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/platform_auth/_mistral.py:55-75]\\n\\n2. Providers are declarative, not a closed list: `ProviderConfig` carries `name`, `api_base`, `api_key_env_var`, browser-auth base URLs, `api_style` (default `openai`), `backend` (`mistral` or `generic`), `project_id`/`region` for Google Vertex ADC, `reasoning_field_name`, `emits_finish_reason` and `extra_headers`. The shipped defaults are only `mistral` and a local `llamacpp` endpoint, so any OpenAI-compatible gateway is a config row. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:137-204] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py:200-214]\\n\\n3. Models are declarative rows too: `name`, `provider`, `alias`, `temperature` (default 0.2), `thinking`, `thinking_levels`, `input_price`/`output_price`/`cached_input_price` per million tokens, `max_context_length`, `auto_compact_threshold`, `supports_images`. Pinning `deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017` and `zai-glm-5-3-flash` is therefore a provider row plus a model row each, selected by `--model <alias>`; Vibe compiles in no roster beyond the single default `mistral-medium-3.5` row. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:522-616] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py:216-231]\\n\\n4. The Mistral-side catalogue is fetched, not shipped: `MODEL_CATALOG_PATH = \\\"/model-catalog\\\"` with surface `vibe-code`, a 5s bounded fetch and a 30-day cache TTL, built from the provider's `api_base`. A dispatch therefore sees whatever the configured Mistral API base advertises, while BYOK providers rely entirely on declared rows. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/model_catalog/_constants.py:1-27]\\n\\n5. Reasoning effort has no dispatch flag. It is a per-model config field: `thinking` (a `ThinkingLevel`, default `off`) plus the offered `thinking_levels` list, with `thinking_is_set` distinguishing \\\"unset\\\" from \\\"off\\\" and the Mistral backend mapping curated level sets to its own reasoning-effort parameter. A governed executor must therefore pin reasoning through the model row or agent profile, not through the command line. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:551-616] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/llm/reasoning.py:17-62]\\n\\n6. The usage counter is the org's monthly Vibe Code allowance. `GET /v1/billing/subscription` names the plan and whether pay-as-you-go covers the run past its allowance; `GET /v1/billing/budget` reports `usage_percentage`, `initial_budget`, `reset_at` and `payg_enabled` for the Vibe Code budget. Both are optional and read as `None` on a self-hosted platform or missing permission. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_billing.py:1-46]\\n\\n7. Plan labels are derived from `/whoami`: chat plans map Free/Pro/Student/Team, Mistral Code maps \\\"Free Codestral\\\"/\\\"Code Enterprise\\\", and API plans map \\\"Free API\\\"/\\\"PAYG API\\\". The label is display data; the budget read above is the counter a dispatch actually draws on. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/setup/auth/whoami.py:346-390]\\n\\n8. Per-dispatch cost is locally computable even without the billing API: `export.json` carries `usage`, `cost_usd`, `steps` and `subagents[].cost_usd`, priced from the model row's per-million rates with cached input billed at `cached_input_price` when set. That gives a governed executor a cost signal per run, independent of the org budget endpoint. [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/run_export.py:117-160,183-190] [SOURCE: ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py:537-550]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Reading `~/.vibe/config.toml` or any key to confirm the live provider: the directory holds only `trusted_folders.toml`, so there is no local provider state to observe, and reading a key value is out of scope by the angle's own rule.\\n- Treating the model catalogue as a shipped roster: it is fetched from `/model-catalog` at runtime with a 5s cap and 30-day cache, so an offline install has only declared rows.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Answering the OpenCode-versus-Vibe counter comparison from client code. Both clients send a key to a provider; which internal counter the platform debits is server-side and unobservable locally. Recorded as UNKNOWN with the exact measurement that would settle it.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"subscription\\\" could mean the chat plan or the Vibe Code budget. Selected the narrow reading: the budget endpoint that the client reads for Vibe Code usage, with plan labels as display only.\\n- Contradictory evidence: `--setup` is described as \\\"Setup API key and exit\\\", while the provider defaults also offer browser sign-in. Both are real paths; the install has neither configured, so no live discrimination was possible.\\n- Missing dependencies: no credential, so the billing read, `/whoami` label and a live model pin could not be observed. Source evidence carried the findings; every live claim is marked unconfirmed.\\n- Partial success: the provider/model/auth contract is fully answered; the cross-runtime usage-counter comparison is UNKNOWN.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/_defaults.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/vibe_schema.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/platform_auth/_mistral.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/model_catalog/_constants.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/llm/reasoning.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_billing.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/setup/auth/whoami.py\\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/app_server/run_export.py\\n- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: Which providers, models and authentication paths can a Vibe dispatch use, and which usage counter does a turn draw on?\\n- Questions answered: Which providers, models and authentication paths can a Vibe dispatch use, and which usage counter does a turn draw on? (Vibe side answered; the OpenCode-counter comparison is UNKNOWN, with the measurement that would settle it recorded below.)\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: starting from the config schema and `ProviderConfig`/`ModelConfig` gave the whole model surface in two files, and `_billing.py` answered the counter question directly instead of by inference from marketing copy.\\n- What did not work and why: looking for a \\\"subscription\\\" flag in the CLI. There is none: the plan is read from the platform, not configured locally.\\n- What I would do differently: capture `vibe config schema` earlier and query it by definition name; it is the cheapest index to every config field, and it was already on disk from iteration 1's capture.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 3: configuration and the repo-local runtime folder. Read the config layer order (`core/config/layers/`), `AGENTS.md`/project-context handling, agent TOML discovery under `~/.vibe/agents/`, and the path resolution module, then state exactly what a repo-root `.vibe/` mirror would contain.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659323459,"end":1794659329517}}}}
