{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659617189,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da0c881e001KvuR2tgo1jlAlD","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da0c7b71001Oz6ierDyWk0Fu2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af743150a46f3b13","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -rn \"eight\" specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/*hook-parity*/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -10; grep -rniE \"guard\" .dsh/plugins/*/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -15"},"output":".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:1:# Repo Guards Plugin Bundle\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:7:`repo-guards/` connects DSH events to the repository's shared guard cores. The entrypoint registers adapters, and each adapter translates event data into a core call and delivers the result. Shared cores keep policy ownership.\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:9:The bundle runs in two compositions. An interactive session, `dsh web` or a headless run with only the guards patch, gets every adapter. A fan-out leaf adds the lineage patch, and its marker row turns off the four adapters that write state or start background work. Everything else, the guards, the context injections and decision capture, runs in both.\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:54:repo-guards/\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:55:+-- index.mjs                 # bundle entry the guards patch loads\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:58:|   +-- ask-surface-guard.mjs, classifier-injection-screen.mjs, completion-evidence.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:60:|   +-- dispatch-audit.mjs, dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs, env-secret-guard.mjs, git-message-gate.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:62:|   +-- mcp-route-guard.mjs, overlay-guard.mjs, post-edit-quality.mjs, prompt-advisor.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:65:|   +-- task-dispatch-guard.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:85:| `ask-surface-guard` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn: a closing typed option menu with no `ask_user_question` call | skipped, as is any headless or child session, since none has a question tool | Log and continue |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:86:| `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | runs | Log and continue |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:88:| `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | runs | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info` |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:90:| `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:91:| `env-secret-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `read`, `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `grep`, `bash` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a call that reads or writes a dotenv file |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:100:| `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | off | Log each failing guard and continue |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:1:# Repo Guards Plugin Bundle\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:7:`repo-guards/` connects DSH events to the repository's shared guard cores. The entrypoint registers adapters, and each adapter translates event data into a core call and delivers the result. Shared cores keep policy ownership.\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:9:The bundle runs in two compositions. An interactive session, `dsh web` or a headless run with only the guards patch, gets every adapter. A fan-out leaf adds the lineage patch, and its marker row turns off the four adapters that write state or start background work. Everything else, the guards, the context injections and decision capture, runs in both.\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:54:repo-guards/\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:55:+-- index.mjs                 # bundle entry the guards patch loads\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:58:|   +-- ask-surface-guard.mjs, classifier-injection-screen.mjs, completion-evidence.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:60:|   +-- dispatch-audit.mjs, dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs, env-secret-guard.mjs, git-message-gate.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:62:|   +-- mcp-route-guard.mjs, overlay-guard.mjs, post-edit-quality.mjs, prompt-advisor.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:65:|   +-- task-dispatch-guard.mjs\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:85:| `ask-surface-guard` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn: a closing typed option menu with no `ask_user_question` call | skipped, as is any headless or child session, since none has a question tool | Log and continue |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:86:| `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | runs | Log and continue |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:88:| `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | runs | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info` |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:90:| `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:91:| `env-secret-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `read`, `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `grep`, `bash` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a call that reads or writes a dotenv file |\n.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md:100:| `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | off | Log each failing guard and continue |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd