an overlay owns |\n91: | `env-secret-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `read`, `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `grep`, `bash` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a call that reads or writes a dotenv file |\n92: | `git-preflight-advisory` | `tools/post-execute` | Bash Git commands | runs | Log and continue, add context |\n93: | `git-message-gate` | `tools/pre-execute` | Bash commands covered by the message contract | runs | Log unexpected errors and continue, deny on `ContractError` |\n94: | `goal-context` | `agent/created` | `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` chat slice | runs | Log and continue |\n95: | `session-start-context` | `agent/created` | Session-prime output | runs | Log and continue |\n96: | `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | runs | Log and continue |\n97: | `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | runs, headless has no question tool | Log and continue |\n98: | `prompt-advisor` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | off | Log and continue |\n99: | `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | off | Log and continue |\n100: | `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | off | Log each failing guard and continue |\n101: | `session-stop-context` | `agent/disposed` | `session-stop.js` autosave | off | Log and continue |\n102: \n103: Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`. Their core errors do not block tool calls. They build injected messages and the goal tool with the harness's own `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`, which `dsh-llm.mjs` resolves from the running `dsh` binary, because this checkout has no copy of them.\n104: \n105: `dispatch-audit`, `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `git-preflight-advisory`, `mcp-route-guard` and `session-start-advisories` find the checkout from their own file, not the session cwd. A dsh session runs in a lineage or scratch folder, where a cwd-relative rule tree would be empty and the lint would allow every command. `git-message-gate` is a policy gate, so a contract violation or unreadable contract returns `deny`.\n106: \n107: `goal-manage` and `session-compact-context` wait for the `commands`, `tools` and `agents` services through `ctx.inject`. A bundle-level `inject` would hold every guard until those services exist, and this cordis build has no optional form.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 5. CONFIGURATION\n112: \n113: The bundle registers the prompt advisor unless its row flag `false` is set. The guards patch still writes `true`, which leaves the advisor on in both compositions. The lineage patch does not change the flag. It mounts its marker row, and a lineage leaf stays without a brief because the adapter returns before it asks the advisor.\n114: \n115: ```yaml\n116: - id: repo-guards\n117:   name: ../plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\n118:   config:\n119:     adapters:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 120]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md, lines 80-119\n80: | `dispatch-audit` | `tools/post-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and continue |\n81: | `dispatch-preflight-lint` | `tools/pre-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and deny on core failure |\n82: | `spec-gate-classify` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and continue |\n83: | `spec-gate-enforce` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `bash` | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and deny on core failure |\n84: | `completion-evidence` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn | runs | Log and continue |\n85: | `ask-surface-guard` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn: a clos