{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794660014778,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da129719002n0uaiVIprG6YMj","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da1288e1001JLI4sa3L6cAgyZ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec403bcd22654d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","oldString":"## Sources Consulted\n\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py","newString":"## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\n- The read-only capture `vibe config schema </dev/null` (stdout redirected into the lineage `evidence/`) caused the Vibe CLI itself to bootstrap `$VIBE_HOME` and create three files outside the lineage: `~/.vibe/logs/vibe.log` (0 bytes), `~/.vibe/logs/vibe-rs.log` (0 bytes) and `~/.vibe/vibehistory` (12 bytes, \"Hello Vibe!\"). No credential, key or prompt was written. The files were left in place: deleting them would be a second out-of-scope mutation. This is recorded rather than repaired, and it is a genuine dispatch finding: a governed `cli-mistral-vibe` executor must pin `VIBE_HOME` to a lineage-local directory, as the DSH runner already does with `DSH_HOME`.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py"},"output":"Edited specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","patch":"Index: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\n+++ specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\n@@ -37,8 +37,12 @@\n - Contradictory evidence: `--setup` is described as \"Setup API key and exit\", while the provider defaults also offer browser sign-in. Both are real paths; the install has neither configured, so no live discrimination was possible.\n - Missing dependencies: no credential, so the billing read, `/whoami` label and a live model pin could not be observed. Source evidence carried the findings; every live claim is marked unconfirmed.\n - Partial success: the provider/model/auth contract is fully answered; the cross-runtime usage-counter comparison is UNKNOWN.\n \n+## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n+\n+- The read-only capture `vibe config schema </dev/null` (stdout redirected into the lineage `evidence/`) caused the Vibe CLI itself to bootstrap `$VIBE_HOME` and create three files outside the lineage: `~/.vibe/logs/vibe.log` (0 bytes), `~/.vibe/logs/vibe-rs.log` (0 bytes) and `~/.vibe/vibehistory` (12 bytes, \"Hello Vibe!\"). No credential, key or prompt was written. The files were left in place: deleting them would be a second out-of-scope mutation. This is recorded rather than repaired, and it is a genuine dispatch finding: a governed `cli-mistral-vibe` executor must pin `VIBE_HOME` to a lineage-local directory, as the DSH runner already does with `DSH_HOME`.\n+\n ## Sources Consulted\n \n - ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/models.py\n - ~/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/config/_defaults.py\n","status":"modified",