{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794660026697,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","part":{"partID":"prt_1da12c71b0021HD0qdRRwuYGSN","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d8ffe2Iv7ljplDZNbln","messageID":"msg_1da12bdd6001xxX3TA6vpuVv9P","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a142adf062762b3e","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, `$VIBE_HOME` holds only that lineage's logs and history, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.","oldString":"**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md"},"output":"Edited specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md","patch":"Index: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md\n+++ specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md\n@@ -151,9 +151,9 @@\n ## Phase Plan\n \n Merge target: `research/phase-plan.md` (written by the merge owner; this lineage cannot write outside its directory).\n \n-**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.\n+**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, `$VIBE_HOME` holds only that lineage's logs and history, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.\n \n **Phase B - Generated `.vibe/` mirror.** Render `config.toml` (providers, model rows with `thinking`, `default_agent`), `agents/*.toml` from `.opencode/agents` + `.skilled/agents`, and point `skill_paths` at `.skilled/skills`; add `.vibe/prompts`. *Handoff check*: `vibe config schema` accepts the rendered config, `/skill-name` lists a repository skill, and a custom agent appears in the agent roster. Cost: low-medium. Why second: skills and agents are near-free parity and make later dispatches useful.\n \n **Phase C - Guard wave 1.** Port the seven `pre_tool` guards plus post-edit quality as `hooks.toml` commands with one shared payload adapter and a `.vibe/state` directory. *Handoff check*: each guard blocks a crafted violating call and allows a clean one, with the spec gate neutralized for child sessions. Cost: medium. Why third: it is the largest parity gain that is actually expressible.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, a lineage-local `VIBE_HOME`, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, `$VIBE_HOME` holds only that lineage's logs and history, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.\", \"oldString\": \"**Phase A - Executor kind (print mode).** Build `cli-mistral-vibe` in `executor-config.ts` and `fanout-run.cjs`, with env prefixes, closed roster, exit mapping and stress fixture. *Handoff check*: a lineage runs one research iteration end to end with `vibe -p`, `export.json` is captured, a `3` exit is scored partial, and the audit receipt exists. Cost: low-medium. Why first: every other phase needs a way to dispatch Vibe.\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/devpass-deepseek/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794660026139,"end":1794660026697}}}}
